  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohd. Zakir vs State Of U.P. And Another on 17 December, 2020 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth",
    "facts": "The instant anticipatory bail application has been filed on behalf of the applicant, Mohd. Zakir, with a prayer to release him on bail in Case Crime No. 651 of 2020, under Sections 272 I.P.C., and sections 60/63 Excise Act Police Station- Tilhar, District- Shahjahanpur, during pendency of trial. Submission is that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272, I.P.C. is unjustified. Offence under section 60/63 of Excise Act is bailable and triable by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged. Applicant has definite apprehension of his arrest by the police. Learned A.G.A. has opposed he prayer of applicant for grant of anticipatory bail.",
    "arguments": "Hence in case of his arrest the applicant is directed to be enlarged on anticipatory bail without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case and considering the nature of accusations and his antecedents as per the Constitution Bench judgment of the Apex Court in the case of Sushila Aggarwal vs. State (NCT of Delhi)- 2020 SCC Online SC 98 and order dated 22.05.2020 passed by this Court in Criminal Misc. Anticipatory Bail Application No.2609 of 2020. 3. That the applicant shall not, directly or indirectly, make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the Court or to any police officer; 4. 5. In case, the applicant misuses the liberty of bail, the trial Court concerned may take appropriate action in accordance with law and judgment of Apex Court in the case of Sushila Aggarwal vs. State (NCT of Delhi)- 2020 SCC Online SC 98. 6.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Hence in case of his arrest the applicant is directed to be enlarged on anticipatory bail without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case and considering the nature of accusations and his antecedents as per the Constitution Bench judgment of the Apex Court in the case of Sushila Aggarwal vs. State (NCT of Delhi)- 2020 SCC Online SC 98 and order dated 22.05.2020 passed by this Court in Criminal Misc. Anticipatory Bail Application No.2609 of 2020. 3. That the applicant shall not, directly or indirectly, make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the Court or to any police officer; 4. 5. In case, the applicant misuses the liberty of bail, the trial Court concerned may take appropriate action in accordance with law and judgment of Apex Court in the case of Sushila Aggarwal vs. State (NCT of Delhi)- 2020 SCC Online SC 98. 6."
  },
